{
  "what": "What the day-start sites compose from the day-start rules every morning, as a table: the overdue tasks, the slipped rows split by each list’s carry-over default into asked, carried to today and carried to the backlog, the silent batches’ targets (each root plus, where its list couples, its actionable descendants), the three reminder groups, and the count that opens the review. Measured from the TypeScript before the port.",
  "why": "The composition exists three times inline — the desktop DayStartReviewChecker, the mobile useDayStartChecks and the mobile dayStartSchedule (for future mornings, count only) — and a frontend that is not JavaScript would write it a fourth time. One question to the core answers it for all of them.",
  "writtenBy": [
    "src/components/dayStartPlan.measure.test.ts — a one-off, run once and deleted. It ran `measuredPlan` in dayStartPlan.contractSupport.ts, which is the desktop checker’s inline block copied verbatim, target collection included, over the day-start rules as they are in the core since #61.",
    "With the port, three rows were changed and three added on purpose (decided 2026-09-13); each says so in its note."
  ],
  "readBy": [
    "src/components/dayStartPlan.contract.test.ts (through the door in shared/dayStart.ts)",
    "crates/cal-core/src/day_start.rs (plan_contract)"
  ],
  "whereItLives": {
    "note": "Inside cal-core, beside dayStart.json."
  },
  "notInThisTable": {
    "the rules themselves": "overdue, carried over, the walk down and the reminder groups are pinned row by row in dayStart.json; the rows here exercise how they are combined",
    "reading the settings": "the per-list overrides, the carry-over default, the coupling and the countdown window travel in already resolved (`lists`, `reminders`); parsing the stored prefs is the next step, with its own table",
    "the gates": "the fire gate, the snooze, waiting for every list’s identity, an empty selection, the cache settle, the app lock and the day marker are the platform’s",
    "the scheduler’s filter": "the scheduler keeps slipped rows whose list says exactly `ask`, the checkers keep everything that is not `today` or `backlog`; both surfaces validate the value on reading, so the two sets are the same",
    "wording, announcements, notifications, the writes and the undo": "the platform’s"
  },
  "shape": {
    "today": "the local wall-clock day the TypeScript ran on (noon)",
    "anchor": "the future morning the scheduler plans for; absent = the live checkers, today",
    "currentUserByList": "the account’s own user id per list; absent = no identity anywhere",
    "lists": "the global coupling and carry-over default, with per-list overrides per field",
    "reminders": "the four reminder knobs, as both surfaces hold them after reading",
    "expect": "task ids in answer order per part, and the count",
    "baseTask": "the Task every case’s task entries are overrides over (the same as dayStart.json’s)",
    "addedWithThePort": "a row the port added for a decision taken with it; not measured, since the TypeScript it replaced answered otherwise"
  },
  "measuredIn": "Europe/Berlin",
